      <h3>Anti-Money Laundering (AML) Compliance</h3>
      <p>
        Katryan Property Services Ltd is committed to complying fully with all applicable Anti-Money Laundering (AML)
        legislation, including the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer)
        Regulations 2017 (as amended) and the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.
      </p>
      <p>
        As an estate agency business, we are supervised by HMRC for AML purposes and are required to carry out due
        diligence on all clients.
      </p>

      <h3>Our AML Policy</h3>
      <p>
        We operate a robust AML policy designed to detect and prevent the use of our services for money laundering or
        terrorist financing. Our policy includes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Appointment of a nominated Money Laundering Reporting Officer (MLRO)</li>
        <li>Customer Due Diligence (CDD) and Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) procedures</li>
        <li>Risk-based assessment of clients and transactions</li>
        <li>Staff training and awareness</li>
        <li>Record-keeping procedures</li>
        <li>Internal and external suspicious activity reporting procedures</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Customer Due Diligence</h3>
      <p>
        We are required by law to verify the identity of all clients before we can act for them. This applies to all
        buyers, sellers, landlords and tenants. We will ask you to provide:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Proof of identity — a valid passport or photo driving licence</li>
        <li>Proof of address — a recent utility bill, bank statement or official correspondence dated within the last
          three months</li>
        <li>For companies — Certificate of Incorporation, Memorandum and Articles of Association, and details of
          beneficial owners and directors</li>
        <li>Source of funds documentation where applicable</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also conduct electronic identity verification checks using a third-party provider. All identity
        information is held securely and in accordance with our Privacy Statement.
      </p>

      <h3>Suspicious Activity Reporting</h3>
      <p>
        All staff are trained to recognise indicators of potential money laundering or terrorist financing. Where
        suspicion arises, we are legally required to submit a Suspicious Activity Report (SAR) to the National Crime
        Agency (NCA). We are prohibited by law from "tipping off" any person who is the subject of a SAR.
      </p>

      <h3>Record Keeping</h3>
      <p>
        We retain all identity verification records and transaction records for a minimum of five years from the end
        of the business relationship or the completion of any transaction, in accordance with our legal obligations.
      </p>

      <h3>Sanctions Screening</h3>
      <p>
        We screen all clients against relevant financial sanctions lists, including those maintained by OFSI (the Office
        of Financial Sanctions Implementation) and other applicable lists. We will not act for any individual or entity
        that is subject to financial sanctions.
      </p>

      <h3>Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs)</h3>
      <p>
        We apply Enhanced Due Diligence to clients who are identified as Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs) or who are
        close family members or known associates of PEPs. This requires senior management approval before a business
        relationship is established.
      </p>

      <h3>Training</h3>
      <p>
        All staff who are involved in regulated business receive regular AML training. This training covers the
        recognition of suspicious activity, internal reporting procedures, and relevant legislation.
      </p>

      <h3>HMRC Supervision</h3>
      <p>
        Katryan Property Services Ltd is registered with and supervised by HM Revenue &amp; Customs (HMRC) under the
        Money Laundering Regulations. Our HMRC Anti-Money Laundering registration number is available on request.
      </p>

